class="q"><div class="qtext">23. What is the typical mortality rate in a well-managed broiler flock?</div><div class="opt">A) Under 5%</div><div class="opt">B) 10-15%</div><div class="opt">C) 20-25%</div><div class="opt">D) Over 30%</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: A</strong> — Good management keeps mortality under 5%.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">24. Which of these is a common external parasite of broilers?</div><div class="opt">A) Tapeworm</div><div class="opt">B) Mites</div><div class="opt">C) Roundworm</div><div class="opt">D) Coccidia</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: B</strong> — Mites are common external parasites that affect broilers.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">25. What is the main advantage of deep litter over battery cages?</div><div class="opt">A) Higher stocking density</div><div class="opt">B) Better welfare</div><div class="opt">C) Lower feed cost</div><div class="opt">D) Faster growth</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: B</strong> — Deep litter allows more natural behaviour and better welfare than cages.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">26. Which of these is a market channel for broilers in Africa?</div><div class="opt">A) Hotels</div><div class="opt">B) Supermarkets</div><div class="opt">C) Open-air markets</div><div class="opt">D) All of the above</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: D</strong> — Broilers are sold through hotels, supermarkets, and open-air markets.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">27. What is the recommended vaccination age for Newcastle disease in broilers?</div><div class="opt">A) Day 1 and day 14</div><div class="opt">B) Day 7 and day 21</div><div class="opt">C) Day 10 and day 28</div><div class="opt">D) Day 14 and day 35</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: B</strong> — Newcastle vaccination is typically done at day 7 and day 21.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">28. Which of these is a sign of heat stress in broilers?</div><div class="opt">A) Huddling</div><div class="opt">B) Panting</div><div class="opt">C) Increased feed intake</div><div class="opt">D) Reduced water intake</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: B</strong> — Panting is a primary sign of heat stress in broilers.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">29. What is the typical live weight of a broiler at 4 weeks?</div><div class="opt">A) 0.5-0.7 kg</div><div class="opt">B) 0.8-1.0 kg</div><div class="opt">C) 1.3-1.5 kg</div><div class="opt">D) 1.8-2.0 kg</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: C</strong> — At 4 weeks, broilers should weigh 1.3-1.5 kg under good management.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">30. Which of these is a key biosecurity measure on a broiler farm?</div><div class="opt">A) Allowing visitors freely</div><div class="opt">B) Using footbaths</div><div class="opt">C) Mixing age groups</div><div class="opt">D) Sharing equipment</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: B</strong> — Footbaths help prevent disease introduction and spread.</div></details></div></div></div>

