v class="opt">A) Sold to neighbours</div><div class="opt">B) Thrown in a river</div><div class="opt">C) Burned or buried deep with lime</div><div class="opt">D) Fed to pigs</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: C</strong> — Burning or deep burial with lime prevents disease spread.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">14. What is antibiotic stewardship?</div><div class="opt">A) Using antibiotics routinely</div><div class="opt">B) Using antibiotics only when necessary and correctly</div><div class="opt">C) Sharing antibiotics with other farms</div><div class="opt">D) Stopping all antibiotic use</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: B</strong> — Stewardship means responsible use to preserve effectiveness and avoid residues.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">15. Which antibiotic is banned for poultry in some countries?</div><div class="opt">A) Oxytetracycline</div><div class="opt">B) Amoxicillin</div><div class="opt">C) Enrofloxacin</div><div class="opt">D) Tylosin</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: C</strong> — Enrofloxacin is banned in some countries due to residue and resistance concerns.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">16. What is a withdrawal period?</div><div class="opt">A) Time before vaccination</div><div class="opt">B) Time after last antibiotic dose before slaughter</div><div class="opt">C) Time to clean the house</div><div class="opt">D) Time to isolate sick birds</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: B</strong> — Withdrawal period ensures drugs have left the bird's system before meat is sold.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">17. Which of these is an alternative to antibiotics?</div><div class="opt">A) Probiotics</div><div class="opt">B) More antibiotics</div><div class="opt">C) Sharing needles</div><div 