ls></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">22. What is a good practice when vaccinating via drinking water?</div><div class="opt">A) Use chlorinated water</div><div class="opt">B) Withdraw water for 1-2 hours before</div><div class="opt">C) Use metal containers</div><div class="opt">D) Add vaccine to full drinkers</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: B</strong> — Withdrawing water makes birds thirsty so they drink the vaccine quickly.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">23. Which of these is a rodent control method?</div><div class="opt">A) Leaving feed on floor</div><div class="opt">B) Using traps and bait stations</div><div class="opt">C) Encouraging wild birds</div><div class="opt">D) Keeping grass tall</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: B</strong> — Traps and bait stations help reduce rodent populations safely.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">24. What should you do with a sick bird?</div><div class="opt">A) Leave it in the pen</div><div class="opt">B) Isolate it</div><div class="opt">C) Sell it</div><div class="opt">D) Kill it immediately</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: B</strong> — Isolation prevents the spread of disease to healthy birds.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">25. How often should you inspect birds for external parasites?</div><div class="opt">A) Daily</div><div class="opt">B) Weekly</div><div class="opt">C) Monthly</div><div class="opt">D) Yearly</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: B</strong> — Weekly inspections help detect parasites early.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">26. What is the withdrawal period for oxytetracycline?</div><div class="opt">A) 1 day</div><div class="opt">B) 5-7 days</div><div class="opt">C) 14 days</div><div class="opt">D) 21 days</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: B</strong> — Oxytetracycline typically requires a 5-7 day withdrawal before slaughter.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">27. Which vaccine is given at day 14 in a typical schedule?</div><div class="opt">A) Marek's</div><div class="opt">B) Newcastle</div><div class="opt">C) Gumboro</div><div class="opt">D) Fowl pox</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: C</strong> — Gumboro vaccine is often given at day 14 via drinking water.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">28. What is a sign of CRD?</div><div class="opt">A) Twisted neck</div><div class="opt">B) Bloody droppings</div><div class="opt">C) Sneezing and swollen eyes</div><div class="opt">D) Sudden death without signs</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: C</strong> — Chronic respiratory disease causes sneezing, swollen eyes, and rattling.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">29. Why should you avoid using antibiotics as growth promoters?</div><div class="opt">A) They are expensive</div><div class="opt">B) They cause resistance and residues</div><div class="opt">C) They don't work</div><div class="opt">D) They are illegal everywhere</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: B</strong> — Routine use promotes antibiotic resistance and leaves harmful residues.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">30. What is the best way to dispose of used vaccine vials?</div><div class="opt">A) Throw in river</div><div class="opt">B) Burn or bury</div><div class="opt">C) Reuse them</div><div class="opt">D) Leave in pen</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: B</strong> — Burning or burying prevents accidental exposure and environmental contamination.</div></details></div></div></div>

