 flock eats 500 kg feed and gains 400 kg, what is the FCR?</div><div class="opt">A) 0.8</div><div class="opt">B) 1.25</div><div class="opt">C) 2.0</div><div class="opt">D) 4.0</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: B</strong> — 500 Ã· 400 = 1.25.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">9. What is a good FCR for broilers in Africa?</div><div class="opt">A) 0.5-0.8</div><div class="opt">B) 1.5-1.8</div><div class="opt">C) 2.5-3.0</div><div class="opt">D) 4.0-5.0</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: B</strong> — 1.5-1.8 is the target for improved breeds under good management.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">10. Which of these is a common cause of high FCR?</div><div class="opt">A) High-quality feed</div><div class="opt">B) Feed spillage and disease</div><div class="opt">C) Cool weather</div><div class="opt">D) Good ventilation</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: B</strong> — Spillage, disease, and heat stress all increase FCR.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">11. What does uniformity measure?</div><div class="opt">A) How similar birds are in size</div><div class="opt">B) How much feed they eat</div><div class="opt">C) How many birds die</div><div class="opt">D) How fast they grow</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: A</strong> — Uniformity is the percentage of birds within 10% of average weight.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">12. If average weight is 1.5 kg, what is the range for uniform birds?</div><div class="opt">A) 1.0-2.0 kg</div><div class="opt">B) 1.35-1.65 kg</div><div class="opt">C) 1.2-1.8 kg</div><div class="opt">D) 1.45-1.55 kg</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: B</strong> — Plus or minus 10% of 1.5 kg is 1.35 to 1.65 kg.</div></details></div><div class="q">