tails></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">22. What is the recommended protein content for broiler starter feed?</div><div class="opt">A) 18-20%</div><div class="opt">B) 20-22%</div><div class="opt">C) 22-24%</div><div class="opt">D) 26-28%</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: C</strong> — Starter feed should have 22-24% protein for rapid early growth.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">23. What stocking density is recommended for 200 broilers?</div><div class="opt">A) 10 square meters</div><div class="opt">B) 20 square meters</div><div class="opt">C) 30 square meters</div><div class="opt">D) 40 square meters</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: B</strong> — At 10 birds per square meter, 200 birds need 20 square meters.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">24. What is a good benchmark for mortality in a broiler cycle?</div><div class="opt">A) Under 5%</div><div class="opt">B) 10-15%</div><div class="opt">C) 20-25%</div><div class="opt">D) Over 30%</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: A</strong> — Mortality should be kept under 5% for a profitable flock.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">25. How can you find industry benchmarks for broiler performance?</div><div class="opt">A) Ask other farmers or feed suppliers</div><div class="opt">B) Guess</div><div class="opt">C) Ignore them</div><div class="opt">D) Use only your own records</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: A</strong> — Farmer groups, cooperatives, and feed suppliers provide standard charts.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">26. What is the ideal temperature range for broilers?</div><div class="opt">A) 10-15Â°C</div><div class="opt">B) 20-25Â°C</div><div class="opt">C) 30-35Â°C</div><div class="opt">D) 35-40Â°C</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary>