s="qtext">26. Which vaccine is commonly given to broilers?</div><div class="opt">A) Rabies</div><div class="opt">B) Newcastle</div><div class="opt">C) Tetanus</div><div class="opt">D) Anthrax</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: B</strong> — Newcastle disease is a major poultry disease and is commonly vaccinated against.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">27. What is the purpose of a footbath?</div><div class="opt">A) To clean boots</div><div class="opt">B) To disinfect boots</div><div class="opt">C) To water birds</div><div class="opt">D) To cool the house</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: B</strong> — Footbaths with disinfectant kill pathogens on boots before entering a house.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">28. How often should you hold a biosecurity meeting with workers?</div><div class="opt">A) Daily</div><div class="opt">B) Weekly</div><div class="opt">C) Monthly</div><div class="opt">D) Yearly</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: B</strong> — The lesson suggests a 30-minute meeting every Monday to review the plan.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">29. What should you do with old litter?</div><div class="opt">A) Spread it near the house</div><div class="opt">B) Compost or burn it far from the house</div><div class="opt">C) Reuse it immediately</div><div class="opt">D) Sell it</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: B</strong> — Old litter can harbor disease, so it should be composted or burned away from the farm.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">30. What is the recommended concentration for a footbath disinfectant?</div><div class="opt">A) 0.5% bleach</div><div class="opt">B) 2% bleach</div><div class="opt">C) 10% bleach</div><div class="opt">D) 50% bleach</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><di