t">C) 10Â°C to 15Â°C</div><div class="opt">D) 20Â°C to 25Â°C</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: B</strong> — Fresh chicken should be kept at 0-4Â°C.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">14. What is the recommended temperature for frozen chicken?</div><div class="opt">A) -5Â°C</div><div class="opt">B) -10Â°C</div><div class="opt">C) -18Â°C</div><div class="opt">D) 0Â°C</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: C</strong> — Frozen chicken should be stored at -18Â°C or below.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">15. Why should you never refreeze thawed meat?</div><div class="opt">A) It loses weight</div><div class="opt">B) It causes bacterial growth and spoilage</div><div class="opt">C) It becomes tough</div><div class="opt">D) It changes color</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: B</strong> — Refreezing promotes bacterial growth and quality loss.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">16. What is a simple way to transport fresh chicken for short trips?</div><div class="opt">A) In a sack</div><div class="opt">B) In an insulated box with ice packs</div><div class="opt">C) In a car boot</div><div class="opt">D) In a basket</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: B</strong> — Insulated boxes with ice packs maintain cold chain.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">17. How much more can processed chickens sell for compared to live birds?</div><div class="opt">A) 5%</div><div class="opt">B) 20-30%</div><div class="opt">C) 50%</div><div class="opt">D) 100%</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: B</strong> — Processed chickens typically fetch 20-30% higher prices.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">18. What is a good profit margin to add to your costs?</div><div class="opt">A) 5-1