ge production.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">23. How long should you smoke chicken to add flavor and extend shelf life?</div><div class="opt">A) 30 minutes</div><div class="opt">B) 2-4 hours</div><div class="opt">C) 8 hours</div><div class="opt">D) 24 hours</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: B</strong> — Smoking for 2-4 hours imparts flavor and preserves meat.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">24. What must be included on value-added product labels?</div><div class="opt">A) Ingredients, weight, expiry date</div><div class="opt">B) Farm name only</div><div class="opt">C) Price only</div><div class="opt">D) No label needed</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: A</strong> — Labels must inform customers about ingredients, weight, and expiry.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">25. Why is it important to rest birds after transport before slaughter?</div><div class="opt">A) To make them gain weight</div><div class="opt">B) To reduce stress and improve meat quality</div><div class="opt">C) To make them easier to catch</div><div class="opt">D) To increase bleeding</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: B</strong> — Resting reduces stress, preventing tough, pale meat.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">26. What is the correct way to restrain a bird for slaughter?</div><div class="opt">A) By the wings</div><div class="opt">B) In a killing cone upside down</div><div class="opt">C) On a table</div><div class="opt">D) By the neck</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: B</strong> — A killing cone holds the bird upside down for a clean cut.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">27. What should you do with clean gizzard, heart, and liver?</div><div class="opt">A) Discard</div><div class="opt">B) Save for sale or