iv class="opt">B) A type of feed</div><div class="opt">C) A record of past sales</div><div class="opt">D) A loan from a bank</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: A</strong> — A budget is a financial plan that estimates future income and expenses.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">9. What does cash flow planning help you avoid?</div><div class="opt">A) Running out of cash before selling birds</div><div class="opt">B) Buying too many chicks</div><div class="opt">C) Selling at high prices</div><div class="opt">D) Keeping records</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: A</strong> — Cash flow planning ensures you have enough money to cover expenses until income arrives.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">10. In the cash flow example, what was the closing balance in week 6 before sales?</div><div class="opt">A) $25</div><div class="opt">B) -$50</div><div class="opt">C) $100</div><div class="opt">D) $0</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: B</strong> — The example shows a negative balance of $50, meaning you need extra cash.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">11. Which of these is a common risk in broiler farming?</div><div class="opt">A) Disease outbreak</div><div class="opt">B) Too much profit</div><div class="opt">C) Low feed prices</div><div class="opt">D) Easy market access</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: A</strong> — Disease is a major risk that can cause high mortality and financial loss.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">12. What is biosecurity?</div><div class="opt">A) Measures to prevent disease entry</div><div class="opt">B) A type of insurance</div><div class="opt">C) A feed additive</div><div class="opt">D) A marketing strategy</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: A</strong> — Biosecurity includes practices like disinfection and limiting visitors to keep diseases out.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">13. How can you manage price drop risk?</div><div class="opt">A) Sell in different markets or process birds</div><div class="opt">B) Ignore the market</div><div class="opt">C) Reduce feed quality</div><div class="opt">D) Increase production without planning</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: A</strong> — Diversifying markets or adding value through processing can reduce the impact of low prices.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">14. What is insurance?</div><div class="opt">A) A tool to transfer risk to a company</div><div class="opt">B) A type of loan</div><div class="opt">C) A government grant</div><div class="opt">D) A savings account</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: A</strong> — Insurance transfers the financial risk of certain losses to an insurer for a premium.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">15. What is a good rule for emergency savings?</div><div class="opt">A) Save 10% of each batch's profit</div><div class="opt">B) Save nothing</div><div class="opt">C) Save 90% of profit</div><div class="opt">D) Save only when you have extra</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: A</strong> — Saving 10% of profits builds a buffer for unexpected expenses or losses.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">16. Which financing option is usually the cheapest?</div><div class="opt">A) Personal savings</div><div class="opt">B) Microfinance loan</div><div class="opt">C) Bank loan</div><div class="opt">D) Supplier credit</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: A</strong> — Personal savings have no interest or repayment obligations, making them the cheapest.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">17. What is a disadvantage of supplier credit?</div><div class="opt">A) It often comes with higher effective interest</div><div class="opt">B) It is free</div><div class="opt">C) It requires no repayment</div><div class="opt">D) It is only for large farms</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: A</strong> — Supplier credit may include hidden costs or higher prices, increasing the effective interest.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">18. What should you do before taking a loan?</div><div class="opt">A) Make a business plan showing repayment ability</div><div class="opt">B) Spend the money on personal items</div><div class="opt">C) Ignore interest rates</div><div class="opt">D) Borrow as much as possible</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: A</strong> — A business plan demonstrates that your farm can generate enough profit to repay the loan.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">19. What is equity financing?</div><div class="opt">A) Bringing in a partner who invests for a share of profits</div><div class="opt">B) A loan from a bank</div><div class="opt">C) A government grant</div><div class="opt">D) Selling feed</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: A</strong> — Equity financing involves exchanging money for ownership or profit share, not debt.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">20. What is break-even point?</div><div class="opt">A) Number of birds sold to cover all costs</div><div class="opt">B) Maximum profit possible</div><div class="opt">C) Total revenue</div><div class="opt">D) Total fixed costs</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: A</strong> — Break-even is the sales volume at which total revenue equals total costs.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">21. If fixed costs are $100, variable cost per bird is $2.50, and selling price is $4.00, what is the contribution margin per bird?</div><div class="opt">A) $1.50</div><div class="opt">B) $2.50</div><div class="opt">C) $4.00</div><div class="opt">D) $6.50</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: A</strong> — Contribution margin = selling price - variable cost = $4.00 - $2.50 = $1.50.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">22. Using the data above, what is the break-even number of birds?</div><div class="opt">A) 67</div><div class="opt">B) 100</div><div class="opt">C) 150</div><div class="opt">D) 40</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: A</strong> — Break-even = fixed costs / contribution margin = $100 / $1.50 â 67 birds.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">23. What is profit margin?</div><div class="opt">A) Profit divided by revenue times 100</div><div class="opt">B) Revenue divided by costs</div><div class="opt">C) Fixed costs divided by variable costs</div><div class="opt">D) Number of birds sold</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: A</strong> — Profit margin expresses profit as a percentage of revenue.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">24. If revenue is $760 and costs are $600, what is the profit?</div><div class="opt">A) $160</div><div class="opt">B) $1360</div><div class="opt">C) $60</div><div class="opt">D) $200</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: A</strong> — Profit = revenue - costs = $760 - $600 = $160.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">25. How can you reduce feed costs?</div><div class="opt">A) Mix your own feed or buy in bulk</div><div class="opt">B) Buy the most expensive feed</div><div class="opt">C) Feed less to birds</div><div class="opt">D) Ignore feed quality</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: A</strong> — Mixing feed or buying in bulk can lower the cost per kg of feed.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">26. Why is mortality important in break-even analysis?</div><div class="opt">A) It increases effective variable cost per sold bird</div><div class="opt">B) It reduces fixed costs</div><div class="opt">C) It increases selling price</div><div class="opt">D) It has no effect</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: A</strong> — Dead birds mean you have fewer birds to sell, so your cost per sold bird rises.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">27. What is a simple tool for tracking profit?</div><div class="opt">A) Spreadsheet or notebook</div><div class="opt">B) A calculator only</div><div class="opt">C) Memory</div><div class="opt">D) Guessing</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: A</strong> — A spreadsheet or notebook allows you to record and calculate income, costs, and profit.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">28. What does a batch record include?</div><div class="opt">A) Number of birds, mortality, feed consumed, weight</div><div class="opt">B) Only sales</div><div class="opt">C) Only expenses</div><div class="opt">D) Personal expenses</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: A</strong> — Batch records track production data essential for cost and profitability analysis.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">29. Which of these is a fixed cost?</div><div class="opt">A) Depreciation on chicken house</div><div class="opt">B) Feed</div><div class="opt">C) Chicks</div><div class="opt">D) Vaccines</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: A</strong> — Depreciation is a fixed cost because it does not change with the number of birds raised.</div></details></div><div class="q"><div class="qtext">30. What is the first step in risk management?</div><div class="opt">A) Identify potential risks</div><div class="opt">B) Buy insurance</div><div class="opt">C) Ignore risks</div><div class="opt">D) Increase production</div><details><summary>Show answer</summary><div class="answer"><strong>Correct: A</strong> — You must first identify risks before you can plan how to manage them.</div></details></div></div></div>

